{
  "about": [
    "Feature registry: the one list of build features, read by cmake/Features.cmake and the tools.",
    "Each feature names its config.h macro. The CMake option is TINY_CRYPTO_ followed by the macro without TC_.",
    "config.h owns the defaults and the dependency rules. A feature without values is AUTO, ON or OFF.",
    "A feature with values takes one of the listed names. A value without a number selects the resource-profile default.",
    "A sub-feature compiles its sources only while its parent is on. Shared sources compile while any listed feature is on.",
    "Core sources compile in every build. Features are listed after the features they depend on.",
    "retired_options maps each retired option name to its replacement. An empty replacement means the option was removed."
  ],
  "core_sources": ["src/common.c"],
  "features": [
